# Anchored, so a *source* directory that happens to be named `build` is not
# swallowed: an unanchored `build/` matches at every depth, and it silently
# ignored a test placed in a `…/bangnidraw/build/` package — the file simply
# never entered a commit, while everything referring to it looked fine.
# `*/build/` covers every module's output; `/build/` covers the root's.
/build/
*/build/
dist/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
local.properties
.vscode/
captures/
.DS_Store

# IntelliJ: the project files are committed on purpose (the maintainer
# works from IDEA); .idea/.gitignore keeps the per-user ones out.

# Real signing keys must never be committed. The checked-in app/debug.keystore
# is a deliberate exception (zero-secret CI signing, docs/decisions/0005).
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
!app/debug.keystore
